# Task
Make `garden` the list of these four base waters (`250`, `180`, `50`, `200`), then return how many beds it has with `length`.

@hint
A list is `[a, b, c, d]`. Count it with `length(garden)`.

@reference
### Lists
```hazel
[1, 2, 3]
```
A list of integers has type `[Int]`.

### List functions
- `length(xs)` how many elements
- `nth(xs, 0)` the element at an index

